# Ratchet for scripts/check_size_mul_sites.py (make lint-size-mul).
#
# Files that still guard a size by hand instead of calling dp_size_mul /
# dp_size_add / dp_size_mul_sat / dp_size_from_double
# (native/inc/doppler/clib_common.h), with how many sites and why. A site
# is one OCCURRENCE of SIZE_MAX -- spelled SIZE_MAX, ~(size_t)0,
# (size_t)~0, (size_t)-1 or the like -- that is in the numerator of a
# division, cast to a floating type, or compared in a floating clause; the
# gate's docstring has the full rule. One spelling read by two shapes,
# `(double)(SIZE_MAX / 2)`, counts once; two guards on one line count twice.
#
# THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. A file not listed may not hold one at all, a
# count left above what its file now has is stale and fails, and nothing
# may be added or raised against the merge base with origin/main.
#
# Format:  <path> <count>  # why
